# db-backup schedule (supercronic; TZ from the container's TZ env).
#
# Twice-daily backups → ≤12h loss window (approved §12.4), 12h apart, both off
# the verify window. Weekly verify-offsite Sunday 04:00, deliberately clear of
# the 02:00/14:00 backups (approved §12.3: off-peak, no overlap).
#
# Off-server-key model: the private key is NOT on this host, so the WEEKLY job is
# KEYLESS (verify-offsite.sh) — it checks existence, size trend, a well-formed age
# header with the right recipient stanza, checksum/size vs the manifest, object-lock
# retention, and manifest row/size sanity, but never decrypts. The full
# decrypt→restore proof is the QUARTERLY manual drill (restore-drill.sh), run by a
# human who supplies the off-server key via AGE_IDENTITY_FILE — it is deliberately
# NOT in this crontab. See README "age identity & drills".
#
# LOCAL-ONLY (BACKUP_OFFSITE=0, README "Local-only mode"): no offsite target is
# provisioned, so the weekly slot below runs verify-local.sh instead — same
# schedule, same HEARTBEAT_DRILL_URL, no separate healthchecks.io check needed.
# supercronic execs crontab lines directly (not through entrypoint.sh), so the
# choice is made HERE, at cron-fire time, not just in entrypoint.sh's dispatch
# (which only covers manual/staging invocations).
#
# min hour dom mon dow  command
  0   2    *   *   *    /app/backup.sh
  0   14   *   *   *    /app/backup.sh
  0   4    *   *   0    sh -c '[ "${BACKUP_OFFSITE:-1}" = "0" ] && /app/verify-local.sh || /app/verify-offsite.sh'
